        ":question/id": "c51262c0-6413-5083-b852-6971681819a1",
        ":question/problem": "Find ${f}^{′}(0)$ when $f(x)={cot}^{4}⁡(3x-1).$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "First, we express $f$ as the composite function\n\n$$\nf={u}^{4},\\,u=\\operatorname{cot}⁡v,\\,v=3x-1.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}=4{u}^{3},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}v}=-{csc}^{2}⁡v,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=3.\n$$\n\nApplying now the chain rule twice, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}v}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =4{u}^{3}\\cdot (-{csc}^{2}⁡v)\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =4(\\operatorname{cot}⁡(3x-1))^{3}\\cdot (-{csc}^{2}⁡(3x-1))\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =-12{cot}^{3}⁡(3x-1){csc}^{2}⁡(3x-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we compute ${f}^{′}(0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(0) & =-12{cot}^{3}⁡(3(0)-1){csc}^{2}⁡(3(0)-1) \\\\  & =-12{cot}^{3}⁡(-1){csc}^{2}⁡(-1) \\\\  & =-12(-{cot}^{3}⁡1){csc}^{2}⁡1 \\\\  & =12{cot}^{3}⁡1{csc}^{2}⁡1\\end{aligned}\n$$"
      },
